# FORGEX (lean)
- Mode: GUARDED only for writing money, schema/migrations, login/authz decisions, or secret/env/guarded files; display/read-only work is STANDARD; one reversible file is QUICK. Never lower; unsure → higher.
- Before coding run `ctxpack.py "<task>" --path <file>` (forgex skill), read only `forgex/context-pack.md`, and say `context: pack <id> · <MODE> · <used>/<cap>`. No Python: follow the skill's manual fallback and say so.
- STANDARD/GUARDED get the JSON contract from `scaffold.py <mode>` (fill values, `validate.py`). QUICK: no contract, no STATE.
- Design before you build. Split the work into small blocks, each with its own check, and start with the smallest working seed.
- Make the smallest change. Run `git status` first and never touch user work. Build only REQUIRED work; note other ideas in one line.
- Read only the files you need. Do not rerun a check that has not changed, and do not repeat summaries.
- Never claim a check you did not run. Tests count only if they call the real code. First slice must walk the real user path end to end.
- Close with `scaffold.py render`, plus at most one `pattern`. For more detail, load the `forgex` skill.
- The task is permission. Ask only before deleting data, real machines/hardware, or secrets. Open files as UTF-8.
